{
  "format": "minilang-notebook",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "sqlite_clusters.mnb",
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cl-intro",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# SQLite Cluster Graphs & Dimensionality Reduction\n\nThis notebook creates a sample SQLite database (**`cluster_demo.sqlite`**) containing both **2D scalar columns** and **multidimensional vector columns** (`8D` JSON arrays and `4D` delimited vectors), then explores them with interactive **zoomable, pannable cluster graphs**.\n\n### Interactive Controls\n- **Scroll wheel** (or **+** / **−**) to zoom around the cursor; **double-click** or **Reset** to fit all points\n- **Click and drag** to pan across clusters\n- **Click any point** to open the **Row Details** inspector showing every column and value for that row\n- **Click legend pills** to toggle a color group (or **double-click** a pill to isolate it)\n\n### Try It in the SQLite Browser Too\nAfter running Cell 1, click **`cluster_demo.sqlite`** in the left file explorer, switch the toolbar to **Cluster Graph** (or click **Plot** on the `observations` table), and experiment with **Direct (X vs Y)**, **PCA (2D)**, **t-SNE (2D)**, **K-Means + PCA**, **Per-Column PCA**, and any **Color** column!",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl-seed-db",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": ":> 1. Create `cluster_demo.sqlite` with scalar metrics, categorical labels, and multidimensional vectors\nlet conn := db::open(\"cluster_demo.sqlite\")\n\nconn:exec(\"\n    DROP TABLE IF EXISTS observations;\n    CREATE TABLE observations (\n        id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,\n        sample_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n        domain TEXT,\n        region TEXT NOT NULL,\n        priority INTEGER NOT NULL,\n        latency_ms REAL NOT NULL,\n        throughput REAL NOT NULL,\n        quality_score REAL NOT NULL,\n        embedding_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n        sensor_vec TEXT NOT NULL,\n        notes TEXT\n    );\n\")\n\nlet regions := [\"us-east\", \"eu-west\", \"ap-south\"]\n\nconn:begin\nfor i in 1 .. 90 do\n    let grp_idx := if i <= 30 then 1 elseif i <= 60 then 2 else 3 end\n    let domain := if i = 90 then nil elseif grp_idx = 1 then \"optics\" elseif grp_idx = 2 then \"acoustics\" else \"thermal\" end\n    let region := regions[(i % 3) + 1]\n    let prio := ((i + grp_idx) % 3) + 1\n\n    :> Deterministic pseudo-jitter so clusters are cleanly separated with realistic spread\n    let j1 := (((i * 37) % 100) - 50) * 0.14\n    let j2 := (((i * 61) % 100) - 50) * 0.16\n    let j3 := (((i * 23) % 100) - 50) * 0.10\n\n    let cx := if grp_idx = 1 then 18.0 elseif grp_idx = 2 then 54.0 else 86.0 end\n    let cy := if grp_idx = 1 then 82.0 elseif grp_idx = 2 then 45.0 else 74.0 end\n    let latency := cx + j1\n    let throughput := cy + j2\n    let quality := 55.0 + (grp_idx * 11.0) + j3 * 2.2\n\n    :> 8D embedding stored as a JSON numeric array (reducible via PCA / t-SNE / K-Means + PCA)\n    let e1 := cx * 0.8 + j1\n    let e2 := cy * 0.7 + j2\n    let e3 := (if grp_idx = 1 then 40.0 elseif grp_idx = 2 then -25.0 else 15.0 end) + j3\n    let e4 := (if grp_idx = 1 then -20.0 elseif grp_idx = 2 then 35.0 else 45.0 end) + j1 * 0.6\n    let e5 := quality * 0.5 + j2 * 0.4\n    let e6 := (prio * 12.0) + j3\n    let e7 := (cx - cy) * 0.4 + j1 * 0.5\n    let e8 := (cx + cy) * 0.25 + j2 * 0.5\n    let emb_json := '[{e1}, {e2}, {e3}, {e4}, {e5}, {e6}, {e7}, {e8}]'\n\n    :> 4D sensor reading stored as comma-separated floats (great for Per-Column PCA)\n    let svec := '{latency * 0.5}, {throughput * 0.3}, {e3 * 0.4}, {e4 * 0.2}'\n    let note := 'Batch #{(i % 6) + 1} · {region} · priority {prio}'\n\n    conn:exec(\n        \"INSERT INTO observations (id, sample_name, domain, region, priority, latency_ms, throughput, quality_score, embedding_json, sensor_vec, notes) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n        [i, 'obs-{i}', domain, region, prio, latency, throughput, quality, emb_json, svec, note]\n    )\nend\nconn:commit\n\nlet preview := conn:query(\"SELECT id, sample_name, domain, region, latency_ms, throughput, quality_score, embedding_json FROM observations LIMIT 10\")\nprintln('Seeded {conn:one(\"SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM observations\")[\"n\"]} rows into cluster_demo.sqlite')\ntable(preview, \"Preview of cluster_demo.sqlite (observations)\")",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl-inline-scalar",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": ":> 2. Direct 2D cluster graph: scalar columns colored by an arbitrary string column (`domain`, including NULL)\nlet all_rows := conn:query(\"SELECT * FROM observations\")\n\nchart({\n    \"type\" is \"cluster\",\n    \"title\" is \"Latency vs Throughput — Grouped by String Column (domain)\",\n    \"data\" is all_rows,\n    \"x\" is \"latency_ms\",\n    \"y\" is \"throughput\",\n    \"color\" is \"domain\"\n})",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl-inline-continuous",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": ":> 3. Continuous color ramp: color the same points by high-cardinality numeric `quality_score`\nchart({\n    \"type\" is \"cluster\",\n    \"title\" is \"Latency vs Throughput — Continuous Color Scale (quality_score)\",\n    \"data\" is all_rows,\n    \"x\" is \"latency_ms\",\n    \"y\" is \"throughput\",\n    \"color\" is \"quality_score\"\n})",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl-multidim-kmeans-pca",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": ":> 4. Multidimensional 8D embeddings reduced to 2D via K-Means + PCA (with cluster centroids!)\nlet api_url := env::get(\"MINILANG_INTERNAL_URL\")\nlet tok := env::get(\"MINILANG_INTERNAL_TOKEN\")\nlet headers := if tok then {\"X-Internal-Token\" is tok} else nil end\n\nlet ws_root := env::get(\"MINILANG_WORKSPACE_ROOT\") or \"\"\nlet cur_dir := string(import)\nlet rel_dir := if ws_root != \"\" then cur_dir:after(ws_root + \"/\") else nil end\nlet db_rel := if rel_dir then '{rel_dir}/cluster_demo.sqlite' else \"cluster_demo.sqlite\" end\n\nlet kmeans_pca := http::post(\n    '{api_url}/api/sqlite/cluster',\n    \"json\",\n    nil,\n    headers,\n    {\n        \"path\" is db_rel,\n        \"table\" is \"observations\",\n        \"x_col\" is \"embedding_json\",\n        \"y_col\" is \"__same__\",\n        \"color_col\" is \"__cluster__\",\n        \"algorithm\" is \"kmeans_pca\",\n        \"k\" is 3\n    }\n)\nkmeans_pca[\"type\"] := \"cluster\"\nchart(kmeans_pca)",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl-multidim-tsne",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": ":> 5. Multidimensional 8D + 4D columns reduced to 2D via t-SNE and colored by `domain` (click any point to inspect all 11 columns!)\nlet tsne_res := http::post(\n    '{api_url}/api/sqlite/cluster',\n    \"json\",\n    nil,\n    headers,\n    {\n        \"path\" is db_rel,\n        \"table\" is \"observations\",\n        \"x_col\" is \"embedding_json\",\n        \"y_col\" is \"sensor_vec\",\n        \"color_col\" is \"domain\",\n        \"algorithm\" is \"tsne\"\n    }\n)\ntsne_res[\"type\"] := \"cluster\"\nchart(tsne_res)\nconn:close",
      "execution_count": null,
      "output": null
    }
  ]
}
